<title>USA: U.S. interest rates mostly lower in latest week.</title>
<headline>U.S. interest rates mostly lower in latest week.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve announced average interest rates for the week ended May 9, compared with the May 2 week, as follows:</p>
<p>   Federal funds rate.................5.55 vs 5.61</p>
<p>   3-month Treasury bills.............5.06 vs 5.15</p>
<p>   3-month commercial paper...........5.70 vs 5.72</p>
<p>   3-month bankers acceptances........5.65 vs 5.61</p>
<p>   3-month CDs........................5.71 vs 5.73</p>
<p>   3-month Eurodollar.................5.69 vs 5.70</p>
<p>   30-year Government bond............6.91 vs 6.98</p>
</text>
